# Explicit, not left to console-setup's own auto-selection -- its
# default FONTSIZE is 16 when unset (confirmed directly in setupcon's
# own source), and Uni2-VGA16.psf.gz (what that default actually
# loads) is missing glyphs for several characters vpinos-menu.sh/
# vpinos-banner.sh's logo art uses (▄ ▀ ▓ ▌ ▐ -- confirmed via a PSF1
# unicode-table parse of every Uni2-VGA* variant), rendering them as
# the font's literal fallback glyph ('#') instead -- a real regression
# reported directly from a screenshot, after console-setup was added
# in the first place to fix a DIFFERENT, milder version of this same
# glyph-coverage problem (the kernel's own built-in font, used when no
# console-setup config exists at all, substituting some other
# placeholder for the same characters).
#
# Uni2-VGA14.psf.gz (FONTFACE=VGA, FONTSIZE=14, CODESET from
# CHARMAP=UTF-8 -- setupcon maps UTF-8 to CODESET=Uni2 automatically)
# is the one variant confirmed, via that same parse, to have every
# glyph this project's art needs. CODESET is also set explicitly
# rather than left to that automatic mapping, so this file stays
# correct even if that default ever changes upstream.
ACTIVE_CONSOLES="/dev/tty[1-6]"
CHARMAP="UTF-8"
CODESET="Uni2"
FONTFACE="VGA"
FONTSIZE="14"
